# Agentic SDLC — CODEOWNERS example (mechanism 10.5). Copy to .github/CODEOWNERS (GitHub) or to
# CODEOWNERS / .gitlab/CODEOWNERS / docs/CODEOWNERS (GitLab) and replace the handles with real
# teams (@org/team) or users that have write access. Procedure: the deployment-pipeline skill,
# references/branch-protection.md.
#
# How it enforces the method:
#   - With "Require review from Code Owners" (GitHub) or "Code owner approval" (GitLab), a change to
#     a matched path cannot merge without an approving review from one listed owner.
#   - One approval from ANY listed owner satisfies the rule. That a Product Owner approved the spec
#     and a Tech Lead approved the plan is proved by the hash-bound rows that
#     spec-lint --check-approval and plan-graph --check-approval read in CI.
#   - The last matching line wins, so keep specific paths below general ones.

# Default owner for everything not matched below (optional; remove to leave code unowned).
# *                                    @maintainers

# Specs, plans, acceptance tests and approval registers.
specs/**                               @tech-leads @product-owners

# The quality bar and the gates: changing them needs a Tech Lead.
AGENTS.md                              @tech-leads
CONSTRAINTS.md                         @tech-leads
.agentic-sdlc/**                       @tech-leads
.github/workflows/**                   @tech-leads
.gitlab-ci.yml                         @tech-leads
.gitlab/**                             @tech-leads

# Protect this file itself.
.github/CODEOWNERS                     @tech-leads
CODEOWNERS                             @tech-leads

# Release and operations records: the Release Owner group.
docs/runbooks/**                       @release-owners
